From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 09:26:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 045/185] segacd: stop one character meaning three different
 failures

There is no cdd_valid bug. Annotating the current object file against
the current symbol table shows it written to 1 on the matching path at
$436, cleared on the mismatching path at $580, and tested by the
scoring at $540. The earlier claim that the two paths wrote different
addresses came from mapping a stale build's offsets, after cdd_outbuf
had shifted every .bss address.

The real defect the same disassembly shows is that the score digit
reports three unrelated states as '0': no packet validated, the
interrupt stopped and the watchdog zeroed the score, and nothing
latched yet. Reading the first when it was the second is what sent the
last few rounds after torn reads and bus contention.

The watchdog now says so: 'q' when it zeroed the score itself, 'S' for
a storm, a hex count otherwise. The command counter loses its top bit
to make room, which costs nothing -- it wraps four times a second.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 618603a..0d66577 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -130,6 +130,9 @@ static UBYTE cdd_stat[10];
 static ULONG cdd_rawbuf[3];     /* aligned: the read below is long-wide */
 #define cdd_raw ((UBYTE *)cdd_rawbuf)
 static UBYTE cdd_valid;         /* last packet checksummed */
+static UBYTE cdd_stalled;       /* the score is zero because the interrupt
+                                 * stopped, not because packets are bad --
+                                 * one character cannot mean both */
 static UBYTE cdd_want_ck;       /* checksum we computed over the packet */
 static UBYTE cdd_got_ck;        /* checksum the packet carried */
 static UBYTE cdd_score;         /* valid packets in the last 16, latched */
@@ -686,8 +689,10 @@ void segacd_int_2_c(void)
     if (cdd_irqs != cdd_seen) {
         cdd_seen = cdd_irqs;
         cdd_quiet = 0;
+        cdd_stalled = 0;
     } else if (cdd_quiet < 255 && ++cdd_quiet >= 8) {
         cdd_score = 0;          /* eight VBLs is six missed packets */
+        cdd_stalled = 1;
     }
 
     /* Two counters that must both be spinning, because between them
@@ -737,7 +742,8 @@ void segacd_int_2_c(void)
         | (cdd_cmd_on ? 0x80 : 0)
         | ((UWORD)(cdd_stormed ? 1 : 0) << 8)
         | ((UWORD)((cdd_ctrl | (cdd_ctrl_ever << 2)) & 0x07) << 9)
-        | ((UWORD)(cdd_sent & 0x0F) << 12));
+        | ((UWORD)(cdd_sent & 0x07) << 12)
+        | (cdd_stalled ? 0x8000 : 0));
 
     if (pcm_countdown) {                /* silence the bell when it is due */
         if (--pcm_countdown == 0)
